# Modelos e artefatos pesados
# As sondas lineares sao entrada de produto, nao artefato derivado: a inferencia as le em runtime e
# sem elas quality e seniority caem em regex silenciosamente. Mesmo caso da taxonomia ESCO abaixo.
# Regra de diretorio impede o git de descer na arvore, por isso `ml/models/*` mais as reinclusoes.
ml/models/*
!ml/models/quality_probe_v1/
!ml/models/text_seniority_probe_v1/
!ml/models/bullet_probe_v1/
# insight_gain_v1 is the one that degrades *silently*: warmup fail-fast covers a missing probe
# bundle, but a missing gain table just restores the guessed insight order with a log line.
!ml/models/insight_gain_v1/
!ml/models/language_detector_v1/
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# Validation reports rewritten by the smoke test on every run — output, not source.
ml/training/reports/

# Dados gerados/derivados — reproduzíveis via ml/scripts/generate_resumes_v2.py (seed fixo)
ml/data/*
# The ESCO taxonomy is a product input, not generated data: inference reads it at runtime.
!ml/data/reference/
ml/data/reference/*
!ml/data/reference/esco_occupations.jsonl
# Test input, not derived data: test_target_fit_dataset_validate_smoke reads this fixture, so a
# fresh clone without it fails a test that has nothing to do with the change being made.
!ml/data/synthetic/
ml/data/synthetic/*
!ml/data/synthetic/target_fit_smoke.jsonl
*.onnx
*.h5

# Dados e artefatos tabulares
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.npz

# ----------------------------
# Logs e temporários
# ----------------------------
*.log
tmp/
temp/